# Build context is the repository root. Everything listed here either bloats the image,
# breaks it, or is a secret.

# The two big ones. backend/venv is several hundred MB of Windows-built packages that
# would be useless in a Linux container and would shadow the ones pip installs;
# frontend/node_modules is not in the image at all (the frontend deploys separately as a
# static site) and would otherwise be copied for nothing.
**/venv/
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/

__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Secrets never go in an image. They arrive as environment variables at run time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# Local-only databases. Production uses Supabase and Qdrant; shipping these would mean
# baking stale conversation data into the image.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
backend/data/chroma_db/

# Not part of the service. The frontend is deployed separately as a static site; the
# tests, the evaluation harness and the dev-only console are developer tooling.
frontend/
tests/
backend/try_it_yourself.py
scripts/*.gs

# git metadata. The commit is passed in as the GIT_COMMIT build argument instead - see
# the Dockerfile - so the history itself has no reason to be in the image.
.git/
.github/

# Documents and tooling artefacts
*.pdf
*.docx
*.xlsx
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.claude/
